Apply after fexcore-guest-memory.patch (FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp,
TranslateGuestOperands). Kero Blaster executes PREFETCH; with translated guest
memory the pass threw "Unsupported translated guest memory operation: Prefetch".
A prefetch has no architectural effect, so the node is removed instead of
reaching a host address derived from an untranslated guest pointer.

--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/Core.cpp
@@
+      case IR::OP_PREFETCH:
+        // MaxPS4: a prefetch is a hint without architectural effect; never let
+        // it reach a host address computed from an untranslated guest pointer.
+        Emit->Remove(Node);
+        continue;
       case IR::OP_PUSH:
       case IR::OP_PUSHTWO:
@@
       case IR::OP_CACHELINEZERO:
-      case IR::OP_PREFETCH:
       case IR::OP_VALIDATECODE:
